Short answer:
Clear everything down to (and including, since you have boots of WW)
medusa's level.  Then decide if you need to go lower, or want to do
something else (sinks/altars/etc.)

Longer answer:

You really need to do the quest next.  If at any point you've got
enough potions of GL, just go for it.  Otherwise, clear out the dungeon
all the way to medusa.  AC -9 should be enough if you're careful.
Don't YAS'D on medusa's level (water creatures/blindfold/nymphs over
water/etc.).  The statue has a chance of having a shield of reflection.
 It ruins spellcasting chances, but gives you an option against black
dragons/wands of sleep/etc, and only takes a turn to put on.

Get the resistances you need.  Either find and eat the right corpses
(and right now I'd be more worried about sleep resistance than fire
resistance) or get crowned.  Having FoD is useful (though at this point
will drain too much mana).

Always keep a means of escape on you (better yet, multiple means).

Engrave Elbereth often (every downstairs, under piles of random
boulders, corridors).  Creating obstacles for the mosters is always a
good idea.

Don't be afraid to retreat.



